IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il41-nouns`
IMPORT `il41-opinions`
IMPORT `il41-general`

-- TESTS for Chapter C (ss 13 to 20), written from the text (Sefer HaChukim 3550 pp. 803-804) before the modules were run.
-- Hand rules: s 13 makes the court inform the Attorney General; s 15(d) bars the Government, the Minister and any other component of the executive from directing the Attorney General in a particular
-- criminal proceeding; s 15(c)(3) sends the account the Minister asked for to the Commissioner where the Attorney General sees harm to an important public interest; s 18 gives 1 January 2027;
-- s 19 says the Law adds nothing to the Attorney General's powers; s 20 requires a decision within 30 days.

§ `Tests: Chapter C`

#ASSERT `s 13 requires the court to inform the Attorney General` `a court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 13 requires the court to inform the Attorney General` `a court` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 13 requires the court to inform the Attorney General` `the Government` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 15(d) lets the body direct the Attorney General how to act in a particular criminal proceeding` `the Government` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 15(d) lets the body direct the Attorney General how to act in a particular criminal proceeding` `the Minister of Justice` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 15(d) lets the body direct the Attorney General how to act in a particular criminal proceeding` `a unit of the executive that is not incorporated` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 15(d) lets the body direct the Attorney General how to act in a particular criminal proceeding` `the Knesset` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15(d) lets the body direct the Attorney General how to act in a particular criminal proceeding` `an incorporated body` EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `the body that supervises the Attorney General for the Government under s 15(a)` EQUALS `the Minister of Justice`
#ASSERT `to whom the Attorney General gives the account the Minister asked for under s 15(c)(2)` TRUE EQUALS `the Commissioner for Complaints against State Representatives in the Courts`
#ASSERT `to whom the Attorney General gives the account the Minister asked for under s 15(c)(2)` FALSE EQUALS `the Minister of Justice`

#ASSERT `s 17 gives the Minister the power to make regulations to carry out the Law`

#ASSERT `the day the Law commences, as its text gives it` EQUALS Date 1 1 2027
#ASSERT `the Law is in force on` (Date 1 1 2027) (Date 1 1 2027)
#ASSERT `the Law is in force on` (Date 1 6 2027) (Date 1 1 2027)
#ASSERT NOT (`the Law is in force on` (Date 31 12 2026) (Date 1 1 2027))
#ASSERT `the Law adds to the powers the Attorney General had on the eve of its commencement` EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `the last day of the 30 days of s 20` (Date 1 1 2027) `the commencement day is not counted` EQUALS JUST (Date 31 1 2027)
#ASSERT `the last day of the 30 days of s 20` (Date 1 1 2027) `the commencement day is counted as day one` EQUALS JUST (Date 30 1 2027)
#ASSERT `the last day of the 30 days of s 20` (Date 1 1 2027) `the count is declined` EQUALS NOTHING

